WEBVTT

00:00:01.086 --> 00:00:03.462
What is the
fu... What is the fu...

00:00:03.463 --> 00:00:05.297
What is the future...

00:00:05.298 --> 00:00:07.550
What is the fu...
What is the fu...

00:00:07.551 --> 00:00:09.176
What is the future?

00:00:09.177 --> 00:00:12.179
Theme song playing

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.932
What is the future...

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.459
- News! Bad!

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.711
We're bankrupt.

00:00:43.712 --> 00:00:47.423
Oh, I borrowed money
to invest in Bitcoin.

00:00:47.424 --> 00:00:50.801
Then the price crashed,
and I sold at a huge loss.

00:00:50.802 --> 00:00:52.261
We're ruined!

00:00:52.262 --> 00:00:55.890
Oh, sorry. I didn't realize
you were watching TV.

00:00:55.891 --> 00:00:59.393
- The tragic impact
destroyed the planet Klarg,

00:00:59.394 --> 00:01:02.313
along with its 50
billion inhabitants.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.191
- In other news, Morbo,
guess what's back?

00:01:06.192 --> 00:01:08.068
- The planet Klarg?
- Nope!

00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:09.820
The price of Bitcoin!

00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:10.905
- Uh, wha?!

00:01:10.906 --> 00:01:14.199
- The virtual "money"
is soaring once again,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.619
leading to a
high-tech gold rush.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.204
- Prospectors are heading
west, where cheap,

00:01:19.205 --> 00:01:21.999
filthy electricity
beckons the desperate.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.835
- This gives me
a desperate idea!

00:01:24.836 --> 00:01:26.420
- Haven't you
learned that Bitcoin

00:01:26.421 --> 00:01:28.714
is just a pyramid
scheme for rubes?

00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:30.507
- Yes, and my plan

00:01:30.508 --> 00:01:33.093
is to exploit those rubes!

00:01:34.095 --> 00:01:38.057
You see, the new mining chips
are made from element 81,

00:01:38.058 --> 00:01:41.435
thallium, a rare
element found out west.

00:01:41.436 --> 00:01:43.562
I plan to actually mine it,

00:01:43.563 --> 00:01:46.607
then sell it to the
Bitcoin "miners."

00:01:46.608 --> 00:01:49.443
It's a sure way to
repay my loan brokers.

00:01:51.988 --> 00:01:55.282
- Yo. We're also leg brokers.

00:01:55.283 --> 00:01:57.201
- Goodbye, Robot Mafia!

00:02:02.098 --> 00:02:06.060
- The Bitcoin mines are using
such colossal amounts of power

00:02:06.061 --> 00:02:08.228
that it's ionizing
the atmosphere.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:11.523
We'll need to land and
drive the rest of the way.

00:02:11.524 --> 00:02:13.901
- I'll set her down
on the Donner trail.

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:21.283
It's a good thing we brought
the oxen. Usually, we don't.

00:02:21.284 --> 00:02:22.910
- I've never been
out west before,

00:02:22.911 --> 00:02:25.996
but I'm learning a lot from
these Borax Kid action books.

00:02:25.997 --> 00:02:27.665
I'm
robbing this vault

00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:30.167
and ain't no ionic
compound gonna stop me!

00:02:30.168 --> 00:02:32.127
Freeze, Maxwell's Demon.

00:02:32.128 --> 00:02:34.672
I'd advise you to drop
those gold molecules.

00:02:34.673 --> 00:02:38.592
The Borax Kid!
I'm gonna pump you full of lead.

00:02:40.512 --> 00:02:43.722
- You know, 'round these parts,
folks don't think things.

00:02:43.723 --> 00:02:45.766
They reckon them. And
instead of an idiot,

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.602
I'll be known as a galoot!

00:02:48.228 --> 00:02:51.689
- Isn't this scenery spectacular, Dwight?
- Uh-huh.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.483
Your mother thought you'd
enjoy some fresh air for once.

00:02:54.484 --> 00:02:56.360
She sure was wrong.

00:02:56.361 --> 00:02:59.113
- Well, anyway, I'm
really looking forward

00:02:59.114 --> 00:03:01.573
to some quality father-son time.

00:03:01.574 --> 00:03:02.826
- With who?

00:03:08.081 --> 00:03:09.623
- Ah, crypto country.

00:03:09.624 --> 00:03:12.251
There's thallium
in them thar hills!

00:03:12.252 --> 00:03:14.671
Priceless, toxic thallium.

00:03:17.048 --> 00:03:18.757
- Um, is this thallium?

00:03:20.802 --> 00:03:23.470
- Oh my, yes! High-grade ore!

00:03:23.471 --> 00:03:25.806
- Um, Professor? Toxic.

00:03:25.807 --> 00:03:28.309
- Relax. They're my
prospecting teeth.

00:03:30.103 --> 00:03:32.980
Oh, quit your
chattering. We're almost there.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.485
- Welcome to Doge City!

00:03:38.486 --> 00:03:42.031
Looks like you got seven
hornswogglers and a galoot!

00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:46.243
- Woo-hoo! We made it!

00:03:46.244 --> 00:03:48.579
- It's pretty lawless out
here in crypto country,

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.289
so put on your
protective headgear.

00:03:54.836 --> 00:03:55.878
Hiya!

00:04:09.851 --> 00:04:13.812
- Kind of old-fashioned for a town
built on high-speed computation.

00:04:13.813 --> 00:04:16.190
- Well, every watt
of electricity

00:04:16.191 --> 00:04:18.817
goes to the Bitcoin
mining computers.

00:04:18.818 --> 00:04:19.985
For everyone else,

00:04:19.986 --> 00:04:23.197
it's practically like
living in the Old West.

00:04:23.198 --> 00:04:25.199
- Old West. Got it.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.077
- Until we stake our
claim and strike it rich,

00:04:28.078 --> 00:04:30.037
keep in mind, we're bankrupt.

00:04:30.038 --> 00:04:33.707
So we'll all need to do
Old West stuff to get by.

00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:35.668
- Old West. Got it.

00:04:46.346 --> 00:04:48.472
- Welcome, friends.
What'll you have?

00:04:48.473 --> 00:04:51.183
- Your freest beverage.
We're very poor.

00:04:51.184 --> 00:04:55.021
- Gotcha. I'll just mix all the unfinished
drinks together and start a tab.

00:04:55.772 --> 00:04:58.440
- She seems nice.
- At times, yes.

00:04:58.441 --> 00:05:01.444
Though her mood fluctuates
like the price of Bitcoin.

00:05:03.446 --> 00:05:05.990
- And don't come back
till you settle your tab!

00:05:05.991 --> 00:05:08.701
Though, I do regret hurting
you. I tell you what.

00:05:08.702 --> 00:05:11.120
Go see the girls in the
back room. It's on me.

00:05:11.121 --> 00:05:12.621
- Girls?
- Yep.

00:05:12.622 --> 00:05:15.499
Delilah runs a house
of ill repute in back.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.584
- "Ill"? You mean a hospital?

00:05:17.585 --> 00:05:18.961
- I mean a cathouse.

00:05:18.962 --> 00:05:20.087
- A pet store?

00:05:20.088 --> 00:05:21.130
- A brothel.

00:05:21.131 --> 00:05:22.589
- A soup kitchen?!

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.925
- Yeah. A soup kitchen.

00:05:31.057 --> 00:05:33.058
- Whoa! Who's that?

00:05:33.059 --> 00:05:36.062
- A psychotic killer,
that's who! Get down!

00:05:36.604 --> 00:05:38.814
- Hey, Roberto!
What's with the piece?

00:05:38.815 --> 00:05:40.524
I thought you were
more of a knife guy.

00:05:40.525 --> 00:05:43.110
- Out here in the West, I
need something shootier.

00:05:43.111 --> 00:05:46.405
Like this gun-knife
I invented-stole!

00:05:46.406 --> 00:05:48.449
Where's that beer I
ordered-didn't order?!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.368
You didn't order a...

00:05:51.369 --> 00:05:54.747
- Say, you're new in
town and low on cash.

00:05:54.748 --> 00:05:58.083
You interested in a job as a
barmaid and/or a prostitute?

00:05:58.084 --> 00:06:02.004
- Um, I'm not sure Leela has
the skills to be a barmaid.

00:06:02.005 --> 00:06:03.256
- Gimme the tray!

00:06:05.842 --> 00:06:08.510
- Alright, up next,
our final item.

00:06:08.511 --> 00:06:10.846
This burro is in
near-mint condition.

00:06:10.847 --> 00:06:14.266
Perfect for hauling Bitcoin,
light housework, or just abusing.

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:15.851
Bidders? Bidders? Do
I have any bidders?

00:06:15.852 --> 00:06:18.103
- Twelve-millionths
of a Bitcoin!

00:06:18.104 --> 00:06:20.689
- Twelve micro-Bitcoin. Do
I hear 13? Thirteen, 13?

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.107
- Not from me, you don't!

00:06:22.108 --> 00:06:25.110
- Fifteen! I always
wanted to own a racehorse.

00:06:25.111 --> 00:06:26.654
- That's a donkey, Bender.

00:06:26.655 --> 00:06:29.156
- Donkeys are just
ugly horses, Amy.

00:06:29.157 --> 00:06:31.367
Sold to the zoologist over there!

00:06:31.368 --> 00:06:34.161
- Oh! I'm gonna call him Rusty.

00:06:34.162 --> 00:06:36.121
- Good 'cause that's his name!

00:06:40.168 --> 00:06:43.003
- Ah! This looks like a
good place to make camp.

00:06:43.004 --> 00:06:45.798
Doesn't it look like a
good place to make camp?

00:06:45.799 --> 00:06:48.592
- It looks stupid. This
whole trip is stupid.

00:06:48.593 --> 00:06:49.843
You're stupid, Pops!

00:06:49.844 --> 00:06:53.263
- I appreciate your
constructive criticism, son.

00:06:53.264 --> 00:06:55.224
- I wish Roberto were my dad.

00:06:55.225 --> 00:06:58.310
He's cooler than a green snake
smoking a sugar cane vape.

00:06:58.311 --> 00:07:01.021
- No self-respecting
green snake would do that!

00:07:07.654 --> 00:07:10.656
Kind sir, could you assay this nugget?

00:07:10.657 --> 00:07:14.618
By my tooth test, I
estimate it's 0.3% thallium.

00:07:14.619 --> 00:07:18.580
- Tooth test?
- Balderweeds.

00:07:18.581 --> 00:07:21.292
Let's see what my
metallurgical analyzer says.

00:07:24.295 --> 00:07:26.338
0.3% thallium.

00:07:26.339 --> 00:07:27.881
- Hoo-hoo, boy!

00:07:27.882 --> 00:07:30.551
I'll give you 100
micro-Bitcoin for it.

00:07:30.552 --> 00:07:33.929
- But weed a million times that
amount or we're gonna get clamped!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.890
Robot
Mafia, huh? Eh.

00:07:36.891 --> 00:07:40.269
Well, maybe there's some thallium
in that there chassis of yours.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.232
- Assay my shiny metal ass!

00:07:47.235 --> 00:07:51.030
0.0000...

00:07:51.031 --> 00:07:53.157
- Tain't even
worth melting down.

00:07:53.158 --> 00:07:55.909
- Well then, perhaps my ass
might be of value to you

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.286
in some other way?

00:07:57.287 --> 00:08:00.080
- Eh, it might make
a good frying pan,

00:08:00.081 --> 00:08:02.708
but fried food makes
me cackle.

00:08:02.709 --> 00:08:04.544
- We'll just sell
you the nugget.

00:08:06.713 --> 00:08:10.716
May I ask who turns the
thallium into microchips?

00:08:10.717 --> 00:08:12.718
- I'm an all-in-one operation.

00:08:12.719 --> 00:08:15.804
My motto is, "He who
smelts it, dealts it!"

00:08:23.104 --> 00:08:26.023
Pop one of those in a
high-end server, and blam!

00:08:26.024 --> 00:08:28.525
You're mining crypto.

00:08:28.526 --> 00:08:31.528
Ooh, lookie there!
Found another Bitcoin!

00:08:31.529 --> 00:08:33.572
Aw, dog dumplings.

00:08:33.573 --> 00:08:35.407
It's just a danged Ethereum.

00:08:39.371 --> 00:08:41.038
- Hello, I'm Zoidberg.

00:08:41.039 --> 00:08:42.915
Like you, I'm a doctor.

00:08:42.916 --> 00:08:45.668
So, uh, what's
your survival rate?

00:08:45.669 --> 00:08:47.961
- Pretty high. I'm
a psychiatrist.

00:08:47.962 --> 00:08:50.673
Got a patient coming 'round
for anger management about now.

00:08:51.675 --> 00:08:55.260
- Hiya, Doc. Boy, it's
been a stressful week.

00:08:55.261 --> 00:08:57.179
What's with the jumbo prawn?

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.431
- A colleague.
Mind if he sits in?

00:08:59.432 --> 00:09:01.100
- Yes, I do mind!

00:09:01.101 --> 00:09:04.228
I value doctor-patient
confidentiality!

00:09:06.064 --> 00:09:07.982
Patang! DOCTOR: Ah!

00:09:19.327 --> 00:09:20.661
- So, how's business?

00:09:20.662 --> 00:09:23.539
- Disappointing. I only
got 30 cents in tips

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.833
and one request to
visit the back room.

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:28.919
I mean, I wouldn't go,
but it's nice to be asked.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.588
Can you think of anything
I can do to look sluttier?

00:09:31.589 --> 00:09:33.590
Nope.

00:09:33.591 --> 00:09:35.259
Look! The Borax Kid!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.177
And his sidekick Mumbles!

00:09:37.178 --> 00:09:40.180
- You know he's not actually a
hero like in his books, right?

00:09:40.181 --> 00:09:43.142
He's a poker cheat and
a low-down base mineral.

00:09:43.143 --> 00:09:45.978
- Wow. The Borax Kid.

00:09:45.979 --> 00:09:47.855
Excuse me, Mr. Kid.

00:09:47.856 --> 00:09:51.442
My name is Fry, and I'm a big fan
of your young adult adventures.

00:09:51.443 --> 00:09:53.736
- Oh, really? Uh,
do you play poker?

00:09:53.737 --> 00:09:56.155
- Yeah, but I was warned
not to play poker with you.

00:09:56.156 --> 00:09:58.407
- Well, then how about a
hand of Colorado Chump?

00:09:58.408 --> 00:09:59.909
- As long as it's not poker.

00:10:02.287 --> 00:10:03.704
So what are you doing here?

00:10:03.705 --> 00:10:06.123
Fighting evil or just
helping townspeople?

00:10:06.124 --> 00:10:07.959
- Not much money
in helping folks.

00:10:08.668 --> 00:10:10.836
Double chump. You lose.

00:10:10.837 --> 00:10:13.630
I heard the
Borax Kid's in town.

00:10:13.631 --> 00:10:15.382
Come on out here, Kid!

00:10:15.383 --> 00:10:17.676
- Mumbles, go see what
all that fuss is about.

00:10:17.677 --> 00:10:20.095
And wear my signature hat.

00:10:23.516 --> 00:10:25.018
Pa-pow-pow!

00:10:29.314 --> 00:10:31.106
- Mumbles is dead!

00:10:32.859 --> 00:10:36.195
Don't argue with me,
Mumbles. I'm the town doctor.

00:10:36.196 --> 00:10:39.865
- Well, shucks. My sidekicks
seem to be dying right regular.

00:10:39.866 --> 00:10:41.784
And in gruesome fashion.

00:10:41.785 --> 00:10:43.285
Care to be my new sidekick?

00:10:43.286 --> 00:10:46.038
- Really? Do I get to
die in your next book?

00:10:46.039 --> 00:10:47.122
- Page three.

00:10:47.123 --> 00:10:49.250
- Then you got
yourself a galoot.

00:10:53.505 --> 00:10:56.006
- Nice camp. Is this my tent?

00:10:56.007 --> 00:10:58.008
- No. You only
come in to tidy up.

00:10:58.009 --> 00:11:01.345
There's just enough room for me
and my private library there.

00:11:01.346 --> 00:11:03.013
- Can I sleep in the library?

00:11:03.014 --> 00:11:05.892
- I'd like to say yes, but
then it wouldn't be private.

00:11:09.479 --> 00:11:11.397
- This place has
too much outdoors!

00:11:11.398 --> 00:11:13.399
It's all bugs and no Wi-Fi.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.526
- Don't get your
dreads in a knot, son.

00:11:15.527 --> 00:11:16.986
Any more than they're
supposed to be.

00:11:16.987 --> 00:11:19.405
How about a father-son
limbo break?

00:11:19.406 --> 00:11:22.117
- I hate limbo, Dad!
Limbo is stupid.

00:11:22.951 --> 00:11:26.328
- Limbo stupid?
Where did I go wrong?

00:11:26.329 --> 00:11:28.455
- Probably when
you took up limbo.

00:11:28.456 --> 00:11:30.958
From what I'm
hearing, it's stupid.

00:11:30.959 --> 00:11:34.336
- Bender! Where are the
shovels I asked you to pack?

00:11:34.337 --> 00:11:35.838
- Oh, you said shovels?

00:11:35.839 --> 00:11:38.090
I thought you said take
a break and do nothing.

00:11:38.091 --> 00:11:40.801
- Hm. Then we'll just
have to find thallium

00:11:40.802 --> 00:11:43.846
the old-fashioned
way. By panning.

00:11:43.847 --> 00:11:45.515
- Panning? With what?

00:11:48.977 --> 00:11:51.895
Sometimes, I
think a detachable ass

00:11:51.896 --> 00:11:55.107
is more a curse than a
blessing. Come on, Rusty.

00:12:00.363 --> 00:12:02.364
We're just a guy with no ass

00:12:02.365 --> 00:12:04.658
And his ass

00:12:04.659 --> 00:12:08.579
Assin' it up under
an asinine sky

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:12.541
Assin' to the
tumbleweeds as we ass by

00:12:12.542 --> 00:12:14.668
Yodeling a cowboy tune

00:12:14.669 --> 00:12:16.003
But, not yet!

00:12:16.004 --> 00:12:19.757
People sass me on
my ass as we pass

00:12:19.758 --> 00:12:23.677
They say, wouldn't it be
better if my ass rode me?

00:12:23.678 --> 00:12:25.971
They tell me I
outweigh my ass

00:12:25.972 --> 00:12:27.890
By a factor of three

00:12:27.891 --> 00:12:30.184
So, I punch 'em
and I kick their

00:12:30.185 --> 00:12:32.728
Yodel-odel-ay-hee-hoo

00:12:32.729 --> 00:12:36.190
harmonizing braying

00:12:36.191 --> 00:12:38.567
Ass, butt, rear-end, ass

00:12:38.568 --> 00:12:40.110
Yodel-ay hee hoo...

00:12:41.696 --> 00:12:44.198
- What the? Rusty!
- No!

00:12:46.451 --> 00:12:49.953
Oh, why didn't I
listen to my own song?!

00:12:55.377 --> 00:12:59.129
- Get yourself tuned or get outta
town, you overgrowed teletype machine.

00:13:00.965 --> 00:13:03.050
- Eh, shut your cackling trap!

00:13:04.636 --> 00:13:06.136
- Cram that racket!

00:13:06.137 --> 00:13:08.932
This is a nice, quiet saloon
with attached bordello.

00:13:10.642 --> 00:13:13.102
- You handle the
menfolk pretty well.

00:13:13.103 --> 00:13:14.812
But mess with my
customers again,

00:13:14.813 --> 00:13:16.814
and I'll kill you in your sleep!

00:13:16.815 --> 00:13:18.273
Lovin' the boots.

00:13:18.274 --> 00:13:20.776
- Um, have you
considered seeing someone

00:13:20.777 --> 00:13:23.153
about your mood swings?
- No!

00:13:23.154 --> 00:13:24.698
But it is a good idea.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.160
Mr. Roberto?

00:13:30.161 --> 00:13:32.538
Folks call me Amarillo Dwight.

00:13:32.539 --> 00:13:35.541
On account of I wrote a
geography report on it.

00:13:35.542 --> 00:13:37.167
Done got me a "A."

00:13:37.168 --> 00:13:40.421
How's about you and me
team up and rob stuff?

00:13:40.422 --> 00:13:42.756
- What are you, like, 11?
- Twelve.

00:13:42.757 --> 00:13:45.759
- Close enough. I need a
kid for a job I'm planning.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.261
See that stagecoach?

00:13:48.346 --> 00:13:49.805
It's taking a USB stick

00:13:49.806 --> 00:13:52.433
with a company's weekly
haul of Bitcoin credentials

00:13:52.434 --> 00:13:54.601
to a bank in San Francisc-y.

00:13:54.602 --> 00:13:57.938
Only, they ain't never
gonna reach San Francisc-y.

00:13:57.939 --> 00:14:00.858
- Why not? They
using Apple Maps?

00:14:04.863 --> 00:14:07.489
Not one patient.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.910
Not even a case of splinters
to treat with my bone saw.

00:14:13.413 --> 00:14:16.415
Thanks, robot, but I couldn't
eat a thing right now.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.086
Can
you save him, Doc?

00:14:21.087 --> 00:14:24.215
- If it's something that
can be cured by a bone saw!

00:14:26.343 --> 00:14:27.885
I'll need anesthetic!

00:14:27.886 --> 00:14:30.137
Get me a bottle
of animal whiskey!

00:14:30.138 --> 00:14:31.139
Ha-ha!

00:14:31.765 --> 00:14:33.807
They see a cute kid
lying in the road,

00:14:33.808 --> 00:14:35.643
stagecoach gotta stop.

00:14:35.644 --> 00:14:37.728
Then I jump out and stab 'em!

00:14:37.729 --> 00:14:38.646
Bang!

00:14:38.647 --> 00:14:41.357
- But, won't that
be, like, murder?

00:14:41.358 --> 00:14:43.525
'Cause colleges look
at stuff like that.

00:14:43.526 --> 00:14:45.527
- Here they come!
Shut up and look cute.

00:14:54.621 --> 00:14:56.622
Guess you ain't as
cute as I thought.

00:15:04.881 --> 00:15:07.383
- The West can be
dangerous at night, Leela,

00:15:07.384 --> 00:15:09.301
so thanks for walking me home.

00:15:11.846 --> 00:15:14.891
Don't worry. The Kid will save
us, right? - Right.

00:15:17.185 --> 00:15:18.686
Better back off, puma.

00:15:18.687 --> 00:15:20.604
- I think it's
actually a cougar.

00:15:20.605 --> 00:15:23.482
- Puma, cougar,
whatever! Get him, Kid!

00:15:23.483 --> 00:15:25.693
- Or a mountain lion. You know,
they're really all the same animal.

00:15:32.993 --> 00:15:35.160
- It seems I bravely
shot that catamount

00:15:35.161 --> 00:15:37.287
just in time after Fry missed.

00:15:37.288 --> 00:15:40.040
- Thanks, Kid. Maybe
I was wrong about you.

00:15:40.041 --> 00:15:43.168
- Beautiful ladies are
wrong about lots of things.

00:15:45.088 --> 00:15:48.215
- Ah, it's nice to see you two
getting along so intimately.

00:15:49.968 --> 00:15:51.677
- It's hopeless!

00:15:51.678 --> 00:15:53.512
There's barely any thallium!

00:15:53.513 --> 00:15:55.889
Just worthless gold.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:58.142
- Well, Rusty's good as new!

00:15:58.143 --> 00:16:00.853
- I performed surgery
on Bender's ass!

00:16:00.854 --> 00:16:02.771
Zoidberg is the hero!

00:16:03.815 --> 00:16:06.150
- No! Bender's ass is!

00:16:07.902 --> 00:16:09.236
- I mean his butt ass.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.283
- It's so beautiful.

00:16:14.284 --> 00:16:16.076
Hey, what's that big rock on it?

00:16:16.077 --> 00:16:19.371
- It's enough thallium
to pay off all our debts!

00:16:19.372 --> 00:16:21.540
Eh, well, mine, anyway.

00:16:21.541 --> 00:16:24.251
- Only the assay shop's
closed for the night,

00:16:24.252 --> 00:16:25.919
and it's getting dark.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.130
- We'll have to take
turns guarding the nugget

00:16:28.131 --> 00:16:30.049
with our lives until morning.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:31.675
I'd take a shift myself,

00:16:31.676 --> 00:16:33.845
but I am already in my pajamas.

00:16:39.601 --> 00:16:43.187
- I steal it. I steal
it not. I steal it...

00:16:44.189 --> 00:16:45.564
- Gimme the nugget!

00:16:45.565 --> 00:16:48.442
And the daisy, too. I gotta
know how it comes out!

00:16:54.616 --> 00:16:56.283
- Ah, nature.

00:16:56.284 --> 00:17:00.204
I hate it. Let's sell that
thallium nugget and hit the trail.

00:17:00.205 --> 00:17:02.247
- Oh, no. The nugget is gone!

00:17:02.248 --> 00:17:04.124
And so is Bender.

00:17:04.125 --> 00:17:06.210
Eh, wha?

00:17:06.211 --> 00:17:08.587
Oh, my gosh! Rusty!

00:17:08.588 --> 00:17:10.839
Bray us what happened!

00:17:14.052 --> 00:17:16.762
Come on! He's picked
up Bender's scent!

00:17:16.763 --> 00:17:18.055
- His what now?

00:17:30.068 --> 00:17:32.487
- Back room don't open
till church lets out.

00:17:34.114 --> 00:17:35.573
It's empty!

00:17:36.282 --> 00:17:38.826
- This is the worst
brothel I've ever seen.

00:17:44.124 --> 00:17:47.084
- It's an immense Bitcoin mine!

00:17:47.085 --> 00:17:49.044
Or an even worse brothel.

00:17:49.045 --> 00:17:52.047
- These aren't servers.
They're robot heads!

00:17:52.048 --> 00:17:54.633
Someone's using them
to mine Bitcoin!

00:17:54.634 --> 00:17:57.845
- That's actually a pretty reasonable
use case for robot heads. But...

00:17:57.846 --> 00:17:59.722
- Hey! It's a guy I know.

00:18:00.807 --> 00:18:02.307
Are you okay, Bender?

00:18:02.308 --> 00:18:05.311
- No, I'm not okay!
That's a stupid question!

00:18:05.312 --> 00:18:07.813
- I was peacefully
stealing your thallium,

00:18:07.814 --> 00:18:09.523
when, suddenly... Ha-ha!

00:18:09.524 --> 00:18:12.234
I was kidnapped by our
friend from the saloon.

00:18:12.235 --> 00:18:15.154
I'm not your friend.

00:18:17.324 --> 00:18:19.492
Though, I
do like you a lot.

00:18:23.747 --> 00:18:26.165
- Didn't you ever wonder
who was gettin' rich

00:18:26.166 --> 00:18:28.417
off all this Bitcoin nonsense?

00:18:28.418 --> 00:18:31.128
- Never!
- Computer servers are expensive,

00:18:31.129 --> 00:18:33.922
but robot heads are
cheap. Heck, free.

00:18:33.923 --> 00:18:37.134
- Mining Bitcoin with
kidnapped robot heads?

00:18:37.135 --> 00:18:39.178
It's pure evil!

00:18:39.179 --> 00:18:43.223
- Hardly. I donate all the
proceeds to a local orphanage.

00:18:43.224 --> 00:18:44.808
Aw...

00:18:44.809 --> 00:18:48.437
- But I can't let you tell
anyone about my generous scheme,

00:18:48.438 --> 00:18:49.938
so I'll have to seal you

00:18:49.939 --> 00:18:52.483
in this comfortably
air-conditioned warehouse.

00:18:52.484 --> 00:18:54.443
Forever!

00:18:54.444 --> 00:18:56.195
But I'll drop by
every day with snacks.

00:18:56.196 --> 00:18:58.365
Aw... ZOIDBERG:
Snacks are good.

00:19:09.959 --> 00:19:10.960
- Huh.

00:19:12.629 --> 00:19:14.713
- Crypto mining was total hell.

00:19:14.714 --> 00:19:16.298
Any number you can think of,

00:19:16.299 --> 00:19:18.842
there's a number bigger
than that!

00:19:18.843 --> 00:19:20.844
- So how do we get out of here?

00:19:20.845 --> 00:19:22.763
- Easy. We'll burrow out!

00:19:25.016 --> 00:19:26.601
Burrow! Burrow!

00:19:28.853 --> 00:19:30.229
I deserved that.

00:19:32.816 --> 00:19:35.067
- This tie pin?
Why, it was a gift

00:19:35.068 --> 00:19:37.611
from my good friend
Diamond Jim Diamond.

00:19:37.612 --> 00:19:40.656
- That guy who's just a
big diamond? You know him?

00:19:40.657 --> 00:19:42.825
- Step away from Leela, Kid.

00:19:43.827 --> 00:19:46.662
The jig is up! I
found your collection

00:19:46.663 --> 00:19:47.997
of Buffalo Bill Cobalt novels.

00:19:47.998 --> 00:19:50.916
You just copied those and
replaced his name with yours!

00:19:50.917 --> 00:19:52.334
- What?!
- Well, now,

00:19:52.335 --> 00:19:53.919
there's nothing
illegal about that.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.338
Those old stories
are public domain.

00:19:56.339 --> 00:19:59.508
I change up a few words and
claim the copyright for myself.

00:19:59.509 --> 00:20:02.636
Ya ever heard of Cinderella?
- That is so evil!

00:20:02.637 --> 00:20:04.847
- I'm calling you out, Kid.

00:20:11.771 --> 00:20:15.274
I told you, stop
that racket!

00:20:15.275 --> 00:20:17.943
- Not till you stop
that damn cackling!

00:20:17.944 --> 00:20:19.862
- Then I'm callin' you out.

00:20:32.959 --> 00:20:34.918
Delilah,
you head-napper!

00:20:34.919 --> 00:20:36.670
I'm calling you out!

00:20:36.671 --> 00:20:38.839
You're on.

00:20:45.221 --> 00:20:47.390
- Look out, Fry! He's
got the ace of spades!

00:20:49.726 --> 00:20:52.228
- That, sir, was
my cheatin' hand.

00:21:09.245 --> 00:21:11.330
- Pops! Get outta there!

00:21:11.331 --> 00:21:14.833
- I'm too scared! There's
bullets in every dimension!

00:21:15.919 --> 00:21:17.878
- Hang on! I'm limboing in!

00:21:17.879 --> 00:21:19.923
You. Play something Jamaican.

00:21:41.903 --> 00:21:43.320
- Your spine!

00:21:43.321 --> 00:21:45.072
It's magnificent!

00:21:45.073 --> 00:21:46.949
- I take after my dad.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.034
Also, I got run
over. Now, follow me!

00:22:00.672 --> 00:22:03.382
- This gun violence has to end!

00:22:03.383 --> 00:22:05.926
Can't we all just
agree to use knives?

00:22:05.927 --> 00:22:07.177
Ha-ha!

00:22:07.178 --> 00:22:09.180
- Well, shucks.

00:22:13.226 --> 00:22:14.351
- Ow!

00:22:14.352 --> 00:22:16.061
- Oops. Sorry, Leela.

00:22:16.062 --> 00:22:19.440
- Ma'am, I'd be right honored
to disinfect your wound

00:22:19.441 --> 00:22:21.860
with the kiss of borax.

00:22:22.902 --> 00:22:25.696
May I escort you to the
brothel, so as you can lie down?

00:22:25.697 --> 00:22:28.907
- I've never been so offended
yet slightly flattered!

00:22:28.908 --> 00:22:30.743
- Then, I reckon
I'll be moseying off

00:22:30.744 --> 00:22:33.246
to plagiarize another
adventure. Ma'am.

00:22:36.583 --> 00:22:39.752
- Perhaps I could
disinfect your wound.

00:22:39.753 --> 00:22:42.839
- I'd like that. Care to
escort me to the brothel?

00:22:45.008 --> 00:22:49.553
- It seems, Miss Delilah, you've
taken a shot to the bustle.

00:22:49.554 --> 00:22:53.182
- Fortunately, it bounced off
your damned thallium nugget.

00:22:53.183 --> 00:22:55.184
Here. It's rightfully yours.

00:22:55.185 --> 00:22:56.603
Oh!

00:22:57.103 --> 00:22:59.188
Well, I'd better
go exchange this

00:22:59.189 --> 00:23:00.814
for Bitcoin, so I can...

00:23:00.815 --> 00:23:02.733
Pay back the Robot Mafia?!

00:23:02.734 --> 00:23:05.737
- Exactly. I'll be
back in a moment.

00:23:09.032 --> 00:23:10.324
- And in the meantime,

00:23:10.325 --> 00:23:13.327
how would you gents fancy
a visit to the back room?

00:23:13.328 --> 00:23:15.954
That sounds like
something we would enjoy.

00:23:18.041 --> 00:23:19.667
- I love you, Pops.

00:23:19.668 --> 00:23:21.877
And limbo is not
entirely stupid.

00:23:21.878 --> 00:23:24.588
- Oh, son. Neither are you.

00:23:28.802 --> 00:23:30.594
- If we ever get outta here,

00:23:30.595 --> 00:23:34.139
I'm gonna give this brothel
a really bad Yelp review.